quartzfire-ssl-inspection (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Per-firewall-rule inspection policies replace the interface-scoped model:
    `service quartzfire ssl-inspection interface <ethX>` is gone, replaced by
    `service quartzfire ssl-inspection policy <rule-number>`.
  * Register `quartzfire-ssl-inspection` with the vyos-1x component-version /
    migration engine (xml-component-version.xml, version 1) and ship a
    config-migrate 0-to-1 script. Upgrading a box whose config.boot still
    carries the old `interface` nodes now migrates cleanly at boot instead of
    failing with "Configuration error" (which left the running config diverged
    from the saved file). The migrator drops the obsolete `interface` nodes and,
    since an enabled model with no policy is rejected at commit, turns
    inspection off while preserving every other setting; the operator re-scopes
    via `policy <rule>` and re-enables.

 -- QuartzFire <cwellman@quartz.systems>  Sun, 12 Jul 2026 13:30:00 +0000

quartzfire-ssl-inspection (0.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: WatchGuard-style SSL inspection — Squid ssl_bump as the
    sole TLS terminator, self-signed inspection CA lifecycle, transparent
    interface-scoped interception, do-not-inspect (splice) list, a plain-HTTP
    CA distribution page on :4126, `service quartzfire ssl-inspection` config
    nodes, and the pre-wired (idle) ICAP content-filter seam.

 -- QuartzFire <cwellman@quartz.systems>  Sun, 12 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0000
